2bek|n|A large cask; an oblong vessel bulging in the middle, like a pipe or puncheon, and girt with hoops; a wine cask. ; A fermenting vat. ; A certain measure for liquids, as for wine, equal to two pipes, four hogsheads, or 252 gallons. In different countries, the tun differs in quantity. ; A weight of 2,240 pounds. See Ton. ; An indefinite large quantity. ; A drunkard; -- so called humorously, or in contempt. ; Any shell belonging to Dolium and allied genera; -- called also tun-shell.	n:lbv,73,1~lbv,73,1	N:15tk,86,5~15tk,86,5
